# Lyam persistent demo - host environment file (deploy/oci/update.sh, docs/oci-deploy.md).
# Run the updater as root (sudo) or as a user in the docker group: it reads this root-owned
# 0600 file and talks to the docker socket. The publish pipeline uses sudo over SSH.
# One KEY=VALUE per line, no quotes, no spaces in values (the file is both read by update.sh
# and passed to the container with docker --env-file). NEVER commit the real file: it holds
# the Bao token and the PostgreSQL URL. This example is safe to commit.

# --- application (required) ---
# The single public origin of the demo (Caddy terminates HTTPS in front of the container).
IAM_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://<host>.sslip.io

# --- application (optional, persistent companions) ---
# PostgreSQL: durable activation journal + decision audit. Without it both stay in memory.
#IAM_PG_URL=postgres://lyam:<password>@pg:5432/lyam
# OpenBao: durable plugin/workflow secrets. Both must be set together; without them the demo
# starts its loopback RAM-only Bao and secrets are lost on every restart.
#IAM_BAO_ADDR=http://bao:8200
#IAM_BAO_TOKEN=<scoped-token>

# --- updater settings (all optional, defaults shown) ---
#LYAM_CONTAINER=lyam
#LYAM_DATA_DIR=/opt/lyam/data
#LYAM_BACKUP_DIR=/opt/lyam/backups
#LYAM_PORT=8080
# Front gate (mandatory): before the container stops, the updater drops this maintenance
# file and refuses to proceed until $IAM_PUBLIC_ORIGIN/healthz answers 503 through the Caddy
# front; it is lifted only when the new - or rolled-back - version answers 200. The Caddy
# site must watch the file (see docs/oci-deploy.md, "Front gate"). Host netfilter rules do
# NOT work here: docker-proxy serves loopback-published ports in userland.
#LYAM_FRONT_BARRIER_FILE=/opt/lyam/MAINTENANCE
# Network shared with the pg/bao companion containers (required when they are set above).
#LYAM_DOCKER_NETWORK=lyam-net
#LYAM_HEALTH_TIMEOUT=420
#LYAM_BACKUP_KEEP=5
# Boot ordering probe budget for host-boot.sh (tries x 5s).
#LYAM_BOOT_TRIES=60
# Cold-backup companions: per-database pg_dump with a FULL application-state capture
# (per-table row count + order-independent content hash, schema-objects hash, sequence
# values; compared after a verified restore) and a tar of the OpenBao storage
# dir plus its unseal-key dir (the Bao container is stopped during the archive, started and
# unsealed again after; a Bao that stays sealed ABORTS the update).
# REQUIRED when the pg backup is set: the compose file of the companion stack (recovery input).
#LYAM_COMPOSE_FILE=/opt/lyam/companions/docker-compose.yml
#LYAM_BACKUP_PG_CONTAINER=pg
#LYAM_BACKUP_PG_USER=lyam
#LYAM_BACKUP_PG_DB=lyam
#LYAM_BACKUP_BAO_DIR=/opt/lyam/bao-storage
#LYAM_BACKUP_BAO_CONTAINER=bao
# REQUIRED with BAO_DIR: unseal key / root token / api token directory - the recovery chain is
# incomplete without it, the updater refuses to run.
#LYAM_BACKUP_BAO_KEYS_DIR=/opt/lyam/bao-keys
# REQUIRED with BAO_DIR: the bao server config (recovery input).
#LYAM_BAO_CONFIG_FILE=/opt/lyam/companions/bao.hcl
# Unseal command used by the updater and host-boot.sh after every bao (re)start.
#LYAM_BAO_UNSEAL_CMD=sh /opt/lyam/bin/bao-bootstrap.sh --unseal-only
# Extra files copied into the private recovery bundle (compose file, bao.hcl, policy).
#LYAM_RECOVERY_FILES=/opt/lyam/companions/docker-compose.yml /opt/lyam/companions/bao.hcl /opt/lyam/companions/bao-policy.hcl
# Optional command run while the container is stopped, BEFORE the local backup - e.g. trigger
# the platform volume snapshot. A failing hook aborts the update (preservation chain incomplete).
#LYAM_PRE_UPDATE_HOOK=/opt/lyam/bin/volume-snapshot.sh
# Freeze updates deliberately (e.g. before a demo): create this file, remove it to resume.
#LYAM_PAUSE_FILE=/opt/lyam/UPDATE_PAUSED
# Host lock against concurrent runs (manual + pipeline).
#LYAM_LOCK_FILE=/opt/lyam/.update.lock
